WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.200
You know the rule for the past.

2
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:05.980
«jouer», «joué». «finir», «fini».

3
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:10.550
«vendre», «vendu». Then you reach
the verbs you use every day.

4
00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:12.570
And the rule stops working.

5
00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:14.620
English has the same problem:

6
00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:18.480
walk, walked. But see, seen.

7
00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:21.970
So the verbs that break the
pattern are the most common ones.

8
00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:25.090
Why is that, and how
can you learn them fast?

9
00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:28.630
In this mission, you'll meet
the rule-breakers one by one.

10
00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:31.800
Then you'll build past
sentences from chips in the lab,

11
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:33.450
and catch the fakes.

12
00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:37.320
Your mission: find out why the
commonest verbs break the pattern,

13
00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:38.690
and learn them fast.
